<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bubastite Portal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bubastite Portal is a gateway in the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, built by kings of the Twenty-second Dynasty, whose family came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a>. Its walls bear a great relief of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Shoshenq I</a> smiting his enemies, with a list of more than 150 places in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> taken in his campaign of about 925 BCE. The campaign is usually linked with the biblical account of Shishak's attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bubastite-portal.jpg" alt="Bubastite Portal" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olaf Tausch · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karnak_Tempel_19.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
